I think this difference between armor and weapons is a deliberate
game balance issue by the DevTeam.

Lots of players go through plenty of amor and weapons and end
up settling on a set for their ascension run and a spare set in the
bag for the highly prepared.  But with armor once you encounter
an item of a type you want in your ascension kit you usually
settle on that piece from then on and focus on the other items.
Two shirts, two body armors, two cloaks and so on and you're
done.  Whatever ones you had before that cost some scrolls but
get one piece of the right type and the variety used goes down.

Because of the number of weapons skills and the different types
of combat strategy, I tend to go through a lot more types of weapon
than armor.  My might enchant a stack of regular daggers a couple
of times before I get enough elven daggers and then enchant them,
but silver daggers are rare enough that I never stop trying to collect
enough for them to replace my elven daggers.  Similar happens to
other weapons - Even if I have Greyswandir and a silver saber
twoweaponed I never stop wanting to enchant some other weapon
of some type just in case.

Weapons go into 4 slots (primary, secondary, quiver, weapon-tool),
armor in 7 slots (shirt, body, cloak, boots, gloves, helmet, shield)
but somehow the number of ?oEA scrolls I'll ever need in a game
maxes out at my main ascension kit, the set of spares I lost in the
bag to an explosion, the set of spares I kept in a box in case of the
explosion.  And the list of weapons I want enchanted is only
limited to how many I can stash in a box - lots.

While the minimum ?oEW is lower, the maximum is higher.  And
so the DevTeam put a tighter throttle on armor than on weapons
IMO.



